  "title": "Unpivot Quarterly Asset Allocation Data",
  "prompt": "A robo advisor stores each portfolio's quarterly target allocation across three asset classes in a wide-format table. The `quarterly_allocations` table has columns `portfolio_id`, `q1_equity_pct`, `q1_bonds_pct`, `q1_cash_pct`, `q2_equity_pct`, `q2_bonds_pct`, `q2_cash_pct` (all percentages stored as DECIMAL). Your task is to unpivot this data into long format with columns `portfolio_id`, `quarter_asset`, `allocation_pct`. Each source column becomes a separate row: `q1_equity_pct` becomes quarter_asset='Q1_Equity', `q1_bonds_pct` becomes 'Q1_Bonds', `q1_cash_pct` becomes 'Q1_Cash', `q2_equity_pct` becomes 'Q2_Equity', `q2_bonds_pct` becomes 'Q2_Bonds', `q2_cash_pct` becomes 'Q2_Cash'. Exclude any rows where the source allocation value is NULL (some portfolios have incomplete data for certain quarters). Order the output by `portfolio_id ASC`, then `quarter_asset ASC`.",
